1
00:00:12,613 --> 00:00:15,652
So why do we learn mathematics?

2
00:00:15,652 --> 00:00:18,200
Essentially, for three reasons:

3
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,828
calculation,

4
00:00:19,828 --> 00:00:21,728
application,

5
00:00:21,728 --> 00:00:24,415
and last, and unfortunately least

6
00:00:24,415 --> 00:00:26,520
in terms of the time we give it,

7
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:28,442
inspiration.

8
00:00:28,442 --> 00:00:30,714
Mathematics is the science of patterns,

9
00:00:30,714 --> 00:00:34,072
and we study it to learn how to think logically,

10
00:00:34,072 --> 00:00:36,599
critically and creatively,

11
00:00:36,599 --> 00:00:39,525
but too much of the mathematics
that we learn in school

12
00:00:39,525 --> 00:00:41,844
is not effectively motivated,

13
00:00:41,844 --> 00:00:43,269
and when our students ask,

14
00:00:43,269 --> 00:00:44,944
"Why are we learning this?"

15
00:00:44,944 --> 00:00:46,905
then they often hear that they'll need it

16
00:00:46,905 --> 00:00:50,170
in an upcoming math class or on a future test.

17
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:51,972
But wouldn't it be great

18
00:00:51,972 --> 00:00:54,490
if every once in a while we did mathematics

19
00:00:54,490 --> 00:00:57,439
simply because it was fun or beautiful

20
00:00:57,439 --> 00:00:59,529
or because it excited the mind?

21
00:00:59,529 --> 00:01:01,251
Now, I know many people have not

22
00:01:01,251 --> 00:01:03,570
had the opportunity to see how this can happen,

23
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:05,399
so let me give you a quick example

24
00:01:05,399 --> 00:01:07,740
with my favorite collection of numbers,

25
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,468
the Fibonacci numbers. (Applause)

26
00:01:10,468 --> 00:01:12,520
Yeah! I already have Fibonacci fans here.

27
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:13,836
That's great.

28
00:01:13,836 --> 00:01:15,952
Now these numbers can be appreciated

29
00:01:15,952 --> 00:01:17,830
in many different ways.

30
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:20,539
From the standpoint of calculation,

31
00:01:20,539 --> 00:01:22,216
they're as easy to understand

32
00:01:22,216 --> 00:01:24,770
as one plus one, which is two.

33
00:01:24,770 --> 00:01:26,773
Then one plus two is three,

34
00:01:26,773 --> 00:01:29,787
two plus three is five, three plus five is eight,

35
00:01:29,787 --> 00:01:31,312
and so on.

36
00:01:31,312 --> 00:01:33,489
Indeed, the person we call Fibonacci

37
00:01:33,489 --> 00:01:36,669
was actually named Leonardo of Pisa,

38
00:01:36,669 --> 00:01:39,722
and these numbers appear in his book "Liber Abaci,"

39
00:01:39,722 --> 00:01:41,372
which taught the Western world

40
00:01:41,372 --> 00:01:44,199
the methods of arithmetic that we use today.

41
00:01:44,199 --> 00:01:45,920
In terms of applications,

42
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:48,103
Fibonacci numbers appear in nature

43
00:01:48,103 --> 00:01:49,960
surprisingly often.

44
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,700
The number of petals on a flower

45
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,562
is typically a Fibonacci number,

46
00:01:53,562 --> 00:01:56,332
or the number of spirals on a sunflower

47
00:01:56,332 --> 00:01:57,743
or a pineapple

48
00:01:57,743 --> 00:02:00,137
tends to be a Fibonacci number as well.

49
00:02:00,137 --> 00:02:03,640
In fact, there are many more
applications of Fibonacci numbers,

50
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:06,200
but what I find most inspirational about them

51
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,934
are the beautiful number patterns they display.

52
00:02:08,934 --> 00:02:11,128
Let me show you one of my favorites.

53
00:02:11,128 --> 00:02:13,349
Suppose you like to square numbers,

54
00:02:13,349 --> 00:02:16,024
and frankly, who doesn't? (Laughter)

55
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,280
Let's look at the squares

56
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,131
of the first few Fibonacci numbers.

57
00:02:20,131 --> 00:02:22,161
So one squared is one,

58
00:02:22,161 --> 00:02:24,478
two squared is four, three squared is nine,

59
00:02:24,478 --> 00:02:27,651
five squared is 25, and so on.

60
00:02:27,651 --> 00:02:29,552
Now, it's no surprise

61
00:02:29,552 --> 00:02:32,380
that when you add consecutive Fibonacci numbers,

62
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,412
you get the next Fibonacci number. Right?

63
00:02:34,412 --> 00:02:35,807
That's how they're created.

64
00:02:35,807 --> 00:02:37,580
But you wouldn't expect anything special

65
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:40,656
to happen when you add the squares together.

66
00:02:40,656 --> 00:02:42,002
But check this out.

67
00:02:42,002 --> 00:02:44,003
One plus one gives us two,

68
00:02:44,003 --> 00:02:46,765
and one plus four gives us five.

69
00:02:46,765 --> 00:02:48,960
And four plus nine is 13,

70
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:52,173
nine plus 25 is 34,

71
00:02:52,173 --> 00:02:54,832
and yes, the pattern continues.

72
00:02:54,832 --> 00:02:56,453
In fact, here's another one.

73
00:02:56,453 --> 00:02:58,297
Suppose you wanted to look at

74
00:02:58,297 --> 00:03:00,795
adding the squares of
the first few Fibonacci numbers.

75
00:03:00,795 --> 00:03:02,403
Let's see what we get there.

76
00:03:02,403 --> 00:03:04,542
So one plus one plus four is six.

77
00:03:04,542 --> 00:03:07,547
Add nine to that, we get 15.

78
00:03:07,547 --> 00:03:09,760
Add 25, we get 40.

79
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:12,551
Add 64, we get 104.

80
00:03:12,551 --> 00:03:14,203
Now look at those numbers.

81
00:03:14,203 --> 00:03:16,587
Those are not Fibonacci numbers,

82
00:03:16,587 --> 00:03:18,466
but if you look at them closely,

83
00:03:18,466 --> 00:03:20,349
you'll see the Fibonacci numbers

84
00:03:20,349 --> 00:03:22,527
buried inside of them.

85
00:03:22,527 --> 00:03:24,597
Do you see it? I'll show it to you.

86
00:03:24,597 --> 00:03:28,330
Six is two times three, 15 is three times five,

87
00:03:28,330 --> 00:03:30,389
40 is five times eight,

88
00:03:30,389 --> 00:03:33,317
two, three, five, eight, who do we appreciate?

89
00:03:33,317 --> 00:03:34,504
(Laughter)

90
00:03:34,504 --> 00:03:36,659
Fibonacci! Of course.

91
00:03:36,659 --> 00:03:40,442
Now, as much fun as it is to discover these patterns,

92
00:03:40,442 --> 00:03:42,924
it's even more satisfying to understand

93
00:03:42,924 --> 00:03:44,882
why they are true.

94
00:03:44,882 --> 00:03:46,771
Let's look at that last equation.

95
00:03:46,771 --> 00:03:50,639
Why should the squares of one, one,
two, three, five and eight

96
00:03:50,639 --> 00:03:53,184
add up to eight times 13?

97
00:03:53,184 --> 00:03:56,145
I'll show you by drawing a simple picture.

98
00:03:56,145 --> 00:03:58,832
We'll start with a one-by-one square

99
00:03:58,832 --> 00:04:02,997
and next to that put another one-by-one square.

100
00:04:02,997 --> 00:04:06,405
Together, they form a one-by-two rectangle.

101
00:04:06,405 --> 00:04:08,954
Beneath that, I'll put a two-by-two square,

102
00:04:08,954 --> 00:04:11,749
and next to that, a three-by-three square,

103
00:04:11,749 --> 00:04:13,750
beneath that, a five-by-five square,

104
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:15,662
and then an eight-by-eight square,

105
00:04:15,662 --> 00:04:18,234
creating one giant rectangle, right?

106
00:04:18,234 --> 00:04:20,150
Now let me ask you a simple question:

107
00:04:20,150 --> 00:04:23,806
what is the area of the rectangle?

108
00:04:23,806 --> 00:04:25,777
Well, on the one hand,

109
00:04:25,777 --> 00:04:28,307
it's the sum of the areas

110
00:04:28,307 --> 00:04:30,173
of the squares inside it, right?

111
00:04:30,173 --> 00:04:31,532
Just as we created it.

112
00:04:31,532 --> 00:04:33,704
It's one squared plus one squared

113
00:04:33,704 --> 00:04:35,937
plus two squared plus three squared

114
00:04:35,937 --> 00:04:38,536
plus five squared plus eight squared. Right?

115
00:04:38,536 --> 00:04:40,393
That's the area.

116
00:04:40,393 --> 00:04:42,719
On the other hand, because it's a rectangle,

117
00:04:42,719 --> 00:04:46,367
the area is equal to its height times its base,

118
00:04:46,367 --> 00:04:48,414
and the height is clearly eight,

119
00:04:48,414 --> 00:04:51,317
and the base is five plus eight,

120
00:04:51,317 --> 00:04:55,255
which is the next Fibonacci number, 13. Right?

121
00:04:55,255 --> 00:04:58,618
So the area is also eight times 13.

122
00:04:58,618 --> 00:05:00,880
Since we've correctly calculated the area

123
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,567
two different ways,

124
00:05:02,567 --> 00:05:04,739
they have to be the same number,

125
00:05:04,739 --> 00:05:08,130
and that's why the squares of one,
one, two, three, five and eight

126
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:10,421
add up to eight times 13.

127
00:05:10,421 --> 00:05:12,795
Now, if we continue this process,

128
00:05:12,795 --> 00:05:16,773
we'll generate rectangles of the form 13 by 21,

129
00:05:16,773 --> 00:05:19,167
21 by 34, and so on.

130
00:05:19,167 --> 00:05:20,576
Now check this out.

131
00:05:20,576 --> 00:05:22,769
If you divide 13 by eight,

132
00:05:22,769 --> 00:05:24,812
you get 1.625.

133
00:05:24,812 --> 00:05:28,239
And if you divide the larger number
by the smaller number,

134
00:05:28,239 --> 00:05:31,112
then these ratios get closer and closer

135
00:05:31,112 --> 00:05:33,765
to about 1.618,

136
00:05:33,765 --> 00:05:37,066
known to many people as the Golden Ratio,

137
00:05:37,066 --> 00:05:39,662
a number which has fascinated mathematicians,

138
00:05:39,662 --> 00:05:42,908
scientists and artists for centuries.

139
00:05:42,908 --> 00:05:45,139
Now, I show all this to you because,

140
00:05:45,139 --> 00:05:47,164
like so much of mathematics,

141
00:05:47,164 --> 00:05:49,131
there's a beautiful side to it

142
00:05:49,131 --> 00:05:51,146
that I fear does not get enough attention

143
00:05:51,146 --> 00:05:52,713
in our schools.

144
00:05:52,713 --> 00:05:55,546
We spend lots of time learning about calculation,

145
00:05:55,546 --> 00:05:58,302
but let's not forget about application,

146
00:05:58,302 --> 00:06:01,756
including, perhaps, the most
important application of all,

147
00:06:01,756 --> 00:06:03,832
learning how to think.

148
00:06:03,832 --> 00:06:05,789
If I could summarize this in one sentence,

149
00:06:05,789 --> 00:06:07,250
it would be this:

150
00:06:07,250 --> 00:06:10,610
Mathematics is not just solving for x,

151
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:13,535
it's also figuring out why.

152
00:06:13,535 --> 00:06:15,350
Thank you very much.

153
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:19,757
(Applause)

